# GitHub SSH Pushes

When a Git/GitHub operation fails with `Permission denied (publickey)`:

- The repository's SSH remote and `~/.ssh/config` may already be correct.
- This project uses `~/.ssh/id_ed25519`, with macOS Keychain integration configured for `github.com`.
- A restricted process can see an empty SSH agent even though the key is valid and registered with GitHub.
- Do not immediately tell the user to regenerate or re-register the SSH key.

First diagnose with unrestricted access:

```bash
ssh -vT git@github.com
```

If GitHub accepts the existing key and authentication succeeds, retry the original Git operation with unrestricted permissions so macOS Keychain can load the identity.

Only propose changing keys, SSH configuration, or Git remotes when the unrestricted diagnostic proves they are actually incorrect. Never modify those configurations without the user's explicit request.
